### Ford Conecta — coleção de requests (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP)
### Rode na ordem, depois de npm run seed. Os logins populam {{admin}}, {{analyst}} e {{customer}}.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@api = {{baseUrl}}/api

### Health (público)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ===================== AUTENTICAÇÃO =====================

### Login admin
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@fordconecta.com", "password": "Admin@12345" }

###
@admin = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Login analyst (pós-venda)
# @name loginAnalyst
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "analista@fordconecta.com", "password": "Analyst@12345" }

###
@analyst = {{loginAnalyst.response.body.accessToken}}

### Login customer (João, vinculado ao próprio cadastro de cliente)
# @name loginCustomer
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "joao@example.com", "password": "Cliente@12345" }

###
@customer = {{loginCustomer.response.body.accessToken}}

### Perfil do usuário autenticado
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}

### Auto-cadastro (público; sempre papel customer, sem vínculo)
# @name register
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Cliente App", "email": "cliente.app@example.com", "password": "Cliente@123" }

### ===================== CLIENTES =====================

### Criar cliente → 201 + header Location
# @name novoCliente
POST {{api}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pedro Almeida",
  "document": "66666666666",
  "email": "cliente.app@example.com",
  "phone": "+5511988887777",
  "city": "São Paulo",
  "state": "SP"
}

###
@customerId = {{novoCliente.response.body.id}}

### Listar clientes, paginado (admin, analyst)
GET {{api}}/customers?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}

### Atualização parcial (PATCH)
PATCH {{api}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "city": "Santos" }

### Admin vincula a conta do App ao cadastro do cliente
PATCH {{api}}/users/{{register.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "{{customerId}}" }

### O dono vê o próprio cadastro
GET {{api}}/customers/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}

### ===================== VEÍCULOS =====================

### Cadastrar veículo → 201 + Location
# @name novoVeiculo
POST {{api}}/vehicles
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vin": "9BFZK54P5J8000777",
  "model": "Ranger",
  "modelYear": 2025,
  "purchaseDate": "2025-04-10",
  "odometer": 500,
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}"
}

###
@vehicleId = {{novoVeiculo.response.body.id}}

### Veículo em JSON (padrão)
GET {{api}}/vehicles/{{vehicleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}

### Mesmo recurso em XML (negociação de conteúdo)
GET {{api}}/vehicles/{{vehicleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}
Accept: application/xml

### Veículos de um cliente (sub-recurso)
GET {{api}}/customers/{{customerId}}/vehicles
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}

### ===================== PREDIÇÕES =====================

### Predição — perfil "fiel" (à vista, garantia longa, maduro)
POST {{api}}/predictions
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "age": 52,
  "monthlyIncome": 15000,
  "vehiclePrice": 180000,
  "paymentMethod": "cash",
  "region": "Sudeste",
  "purchaseChannel": "dealership",
  "hasTradeIn": true,
  "warrantyMonths": 48
}

### Predição — perfil "abandono" (financiado, esticado, garantia mínima)
POST {{api}}/predictions
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "age": 24,
  "monthlyIncome": 4000,
  "vehiclePrice": 120000,
  "paymentMethod": "financing",
  "region": "Sudeste",
  "purchaseChannel": "online",
  "hasTradeIn": false,
  "warrantyMonths": 6
}

### Lista de risco (Cockpit) — maior risco primeiro
GET {{api}}/predictions?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}

### Histórico de predições do cliente (sub-recurso)
GET {{api}}/customers/{{customerId}}/predictions
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}

### ===================== ERROS E ACESSO NEGADO =====================

### 401 — sem token
GET {{api}}/customers

### 403 — customer tentando listar todos os clientes
GET {{api}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}

### 403 — customer tentando ver o cliente de outra pessoa
GET {{api}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer}}

### 403 — analyst tentando remover (só admin)
DELETE {{api}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}

### 400 — validação (CPF inválido, e-mail inválido, campos faltando)
POST {{api}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "x", "document": "123", "email": "naoémail" }

### 400 — feature de comportamento futuro na predição (anti data leakage)
POST {{api}}/predictions
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}", "age": 30, "monthlyIncome": 5000, "vehiclePrice": 90000,
  "paymentMethod": "cash", "region": "Sul", "purchaseChannel": "dealership",
  "hasTradeIn": false, "warrantyMonths": 24, "revisionsDone": 3
}

### 404 — recurso inexistente
GET {{api}}/customers/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}

### 406 — formato não suportado
GET {{api}}/vehicles/{{vehicleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}
Accept: text/csv

### 409 — CPF duplicado
POST {{api}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Pedro Almeida", "document": "66666666666", "email": "p@example.com", "city": "SP", "state": "SP" }

### 204 — remoção (admin)
DELETE {{api}}/vehicles/{{vehicleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
